# This site has no server-side code and needs no secrets to build or run.
# This file exists so that if you add a third-party service later (e.g. a
# form backend like Formspree, Web3Forms, or a static analytics provider),
# you have a documented, safe place to put its PUBLIC configuration.
#
# RULES:
# - Never put private API keys, tokens, or passwords in variables prefixed
#   PUBLIC_ — anything with that prefix is bundled into the client-side
#   JavaScript and visible to every visitor.
# - Never commit a real .env file. Only .env.example (with names, no values)
#   belongs in git — .gitignore already excludes .env.

# Example: public form endpoint ID for a service like Formspree (see
# src/pages/contact.astro for where this would be wired in).
# PUBLIC_CONTACT_FORM_ENDPOINT=
